# Keeps every real secret file off the Docker build context entirely — this is the actual
# control point for "images are environment-agnostic" (docs/plans/deploy-dev.md): Next.js's
# standalone output copies any `.env*` file it finds next to the app at BUILD time into the
# image, so if a real `.env` ever reached the build context, whatever secrets were in it on the
# machine that ran `docker build` would ship inside the image layer. `.env.example` files carry
# no secrets and aren't needed by the build either way.
.env*

node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
**/.next
.next-e2e
**/.next-e2e
.next-deploy-regression-test
**/.next-deploy-regression-test
.next-cron-auth-test
**/.next-cron-auth-test
.turbo
**/.turbo

.git

playwright-report
test-results
blob-report
**/playwright-report
**/test-results
**/blob-report

*.log
.DS_Store
**/*.tsbuildinfo
